.TH SONDA 1 "@DATE@" "sonda @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sonda \- network quality of experience probe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sonda
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sonda
is an experimental network probe.
It measures STUN, DNS over UDP, DNS over HTTPS, and HTTPS, and
stores the raw results in a local spool.
It then archives the raw events into daily files for later analysis.
.PP
The Debian package installs a systemd timer that runs
.B sonda scan
five minutes after the previous scan finishes.
Each scan runs the workflows in
.I /etc/sonda/scan/
that are due according to their cadence.
A long\-running
.B sonda etl\-ptnop\-archive
service archives the events of each new spool entry.
A second timer runs
.B sonda spool\-gc
every hour to remove old spool entries.
.PP
This tool is under active development and its interface may change.
For the full list of commands and per\-command help, run:
.PP
.RS 4
.B sonda \-\-help
.br
.BI "sonda " command " \-\-help"
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sonda/config.toml
Settings for the
.B sonda
commands, such as the maximum age of spool entries.
The commented\-out values are the defaults.
.TP
.I /etc/sonda/scan/*.yml
Workflows executed by the periodic scan.
.TP
.I /var/spool/sonda/
Spool with one directory per measurement, containing the request,
stdout, stderr, and exit code.
The spool garbage collection removes entries older than six hours
by default.
Members of the
.B _sonda
group can read it.
.TP
.I /var/lib/sonda/archive/
Daily archive of ptnop events, written as
.IR \%ptnop/YYYYMMDDT000000Z.jsonl ,
and compressed as
.IR \%ptnop/YYYYMMDDT000000Z.jsonl.zst
once no more data can be appended.
Files older than 90 days are removed by default.
Members of the
.B _sonda
group can read them.
.TP
.I /run/sonda/serve\-ptnop/sock
Socket served by
.BR sonda\-serve\-ptnop ,
which accepts ptnop measurement requests.
Members of the
.B _sonda
group can connect to it.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/sonda/
The
.B sonda
executable and its plugins.
.TP
.I /usr/share/sonda/plugins/
Plugin descriptions shown by
.BR "sonda \-\-help" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SONDA_ETC_PATH
Directory containing
.I config.toml
(default:
.IR /etc/sonda ).
When empty, no config file is read.
.TP
.B SONDA_EXEC_PATH
Directory containing the executable and its plugins
(default:
.IR /usr/libexec/sonda ).
.TP
.B SONDA_SHARE_PATH
Directory containing the plugin descriptions
(default:
.IR /usr/share/sonda ).
